    <div class="by-card by-mt">
      <div class="by-chead"><span class="by-num">02</span><h2>Buy peer to peer</h2></div>
      <p class="by-how">You buy from another person instead of a company, either through a marketplace that holds the coins in escrow while payment clears, or face to face for cash. The appeal is that a private seller does not run a compliance department, so a peer to peer trade can carry far less identity than an exchange account. The cost is that you are the one judging the counterparty.</p>
      <div class="by-rows">
        <div class="by-row by-cost"><b>What it costs</b><span>Usually a worse price than an exchange. The seller is charging for convenience, risk, and their own time, and that premium widens as the trade gets more private.</span></div>
        <div class="by-row by-need"><b>What it takes</b><span>Discipline about escrow and order of operations, plus a wallet address you control on hand. <a href="/learn/no-kyc">No-KYC bitcoin</a> covers the real trade-offs, including the ones people underestimate.</span></div>
        <div class="by-row by-watch"><b>Watch for</b><span>Reversible payment methods, sellers who want you to move off the marketplace, and anyone offering a price far below market. Tax and reporting obligations do not disappear because a trade was private; see the <a href="/terms">terms</a>.</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="by-wlab">Where to go</div>
