    <div class="by-card by-mt">
      <div class="by-chead"><span class="by-num">04</span><h2>Earn it directly</h2></div>
      <p class="by-how">The route with no order book. Invoice a client in bitcoin, sell something for it, take part of a paycheck in it through a payroll service that offers the option, or accept it in a business you already run. The coins can land straight in a wallet you control, with no exchange account in between and no withdrawal step to forget.</p>
      <div class="by-rows">
        <div class="by-row by-cost"><b>What it costs</b><span>No purchase spread. What you give up is timing: you receive bitcoin when you get paid, at whatever the rate is that day.</span></div>
        <div class="by-row by-need"><b>What it takes</b><span>A counterparty willing to pay in bitcoin, and an address or Lightning invoice to give them. Have the <a href="/wallets">wallet</a> ready first.</span></div>
        <div class="by-row by-watch"><b>Watch for</b><span>Record keeping. Bitcoin received as income is income in most places, valued at the time you received it, and nothing on this page is tax advice.</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="by-wlab">Where to go</div>
      <div class="by-svcs">
