        <div class="by-svc">
          <a class="by-logo" href="https://lolli.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/img/buy/lolli.ico" alt="" width="30" height="30" loading="lazy"></a>
          <div class="by-svcm">
            <div class="by-svct"><b><a href="https://lolli.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lolli</a></b><span class="by-since">Since 2018</span></div>
            <p class="by-svcp">Browser extension and app that pays bitcoin rewards for shopping at big-name retailers.</p>
          </div>
          <a class="by-open" href="https://lolli.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open &#8599;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="by-svc">
          <a class="by-logo" href="https://stacker.news" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/img/buy/stackernews.png" alt="" width="30" height="30" loading="lazy"></a>
          <div class="by-svcm">
            <div class="by-svct"><b><a href="https://stacker.news" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stacker News</a></b><span class="by-since">Since 2021</span></div>
            <p class="by-svcp">Forum that pays sats for posts people find valuable; small amounts, real practice receiving.</p>
          </div>
          <a class="by-open" href="https://stacker.news" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open &#8599;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="by-card by-mt">
      <div class="by-tlab">What to expect, whichever route you take</div>
      <div class="by-cols">
        <div class="by-col">
          <div class="by-clab">Identity checks</div>
          <p class="by-cp">Regulated services collect identity before they let you trade, and they keep it. Once you withdraw, that identity is linked to the address the coins went to, and the ledger keeps that link permanently. This is not a reason to avoid exchanges; it is a reason to know what is recorded. The <a href="/learn/privacy">privacy guide</a> covers what follows a coin around, and <a href="/learn/no-kyc">no-KYC bitcoin</a> covers the alternative and its costs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="by-col">
          <div class="by-clab">Spread versus commission</div>
          <p class="by-cp">A commission is a number on the receipt. A spread is a markup inside the price you were quoted, and it does not appear as a line item at all. Judging cost by the fee line alone is how a service with no commission ends up costing more than one charging a stated percentage. Take the quoted total, divide by the coins you receive, and compare that against the <a href="/price">market rate</a> using the <a href="/convert">converter</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="by-habit">
        <div class="by-clab by-clab-acc">The standing habit: withdraw after buying</div>
        <p class="by-cp">Buying is one step. Withdrawing to a wallet whose keys you hold is the step that makes the coins yours, and it is the one people skip. Do it as part of the purchase, not as a project for later.</p>
        <ul class="by-list">
          <li><b>Have the wallet before the order.</b> A withdrawal you cannot complete is a withdrawal that stays undone. <a href="/wallets">Wallets</a> covers the choices; <a href="/learn/self-custody">self-custody</a> covers the seed phrase and the backup.</li>
          <li><b>Copy the address from the wallet, every time.</b> Never from a message or a history list. The <a href="/tools/validate">address validator</a> confirms an address is at least well formed, and <a href="/learn/address-poisoning">address poisoning</a> explains why the check matters.</li>
          <li><b>Budget the network fee.</b> Withdrawals pay an on-chain fee, so many small ones cost more than one larger one. <a href="/fees">Current fee levels</a> are on the fee page.</li>
          <li><b>Do not leave a balance behind for convenience.</b> Custodial balances have been frozen, delayed, and lost with the company holding them; see <a href="/learn/frozen-deposits">frozen deposits</a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>


    <div class="by-about doc-prose">
      <p>Buying bitcoin comes down to four routes and one habit. Exchanges are the common path and cost the least in fees, at the price of identity checks that stay on file. Peer to peer trades less of that identity for a wider spread and more responsibility. Machines are quick and expensive. Earning it skips the purchase entirely. The habit is the same in all four: get the coins into a wallet whose keys you hold, and confirm the address before you send. If you are buying a fixed amount on a schedule, the <a href="/dca">averaging calculator</a> shows how that plays out historically, and the <a href="/price">price page</a> gives you the rate to check any quote against.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
